WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.540
The U.S. is launching airstrikes right now
in Northern Iraq in response to the militant

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.710
group ISIS, which as been controlling parts
of Northern Iraq for months now. President

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.610
Obama, who had worked so hard to pull the
U.S. out of Iraq, authorized airstrikes against

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:20.649
ISIS if it threatens Irbil, which is the capital
of the Kurdish region in the North, or if

00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:25.269
it threatens Mount Sinjar where thousands
of an ethno-religious minority called the

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:30.349
Yazidi are hiding out from ISIS. And this
seems like a really good thing for the Iraqis

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:34.579
who are behind Obama's red line around the
Kurdish region, but the thing is is that most

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:39.399
Iraqis are not behind that red line. Most
Iraqis in Northern Iraq have been living under

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.469
ISIS's rule for 2 months. There's no sign
that President Obama's airstrikes are going

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:48.570
to push ISIS back from there. So why did Obama
do this? Why did he draw a red line that just

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:52.159
protects a tiny sliver of the country and
not the rest of the country that has already

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:57.289
been conquered by this awful group. The first
reason is that the Kurdish region in Northern

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:02.769
Iraq is semi-autonomous. It has a stable government
of its own. It has a strong military that

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:07.320
has been pretty good at keeping out ISIS forces.
There are a number of Americans based there.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.750
But the Iraqi government based in Baghdad
is a complete mess. The military deserted

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:17.380
en masse when ISIS invaded. The civilian government
has been on the verge of collapse for months.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.920
America does not like the prime minister very
much, who they think has been making the crisis

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.729
worse. So Obama's calculation, which is cold
but probably correct is that he can save the

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.090
Kurdish region in the north, but there's probably
nothing he can do for the rest of Iraq. Good

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:36.420
news for some Iraqis, but for the many millions
who have spent the last few months under rule

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.500
by ISIS, there is no end in sight.

